/ref 17592186174253 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186174250 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186174254 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186174250 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186174255 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186174250 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186174250 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186174250 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "abec5dd2-1828-564c-a9d9-a271e1a83367" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186174251 #edb/ref 1080 "$450$ minutes" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186174251 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186174251 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9113f5cc-4e4a-55c9-a30b-3712cb679eb9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186174252 #edb/ref 1080 "$120$ minutes" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186174252 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186174252 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ac3e9265-8dd9-5723-849b-619654aaf8db" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186174253 #edb/ref 1080 "$100$ minutes" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186174253 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186174253 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c6ee89d3-cbb9-550b-98ff-91595829e884" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186174254 #edb/ref 1080 "$90$ minutes" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186174254 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186174254 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d7d15e74-1b02-5c36-929c-6d4519d6370b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186174255 #edb/ref 1080 "$4.5$ minutes" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186174255 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186174255 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "32eb904b-cff0-5901-9a71-62aa54dbc14b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175885 #edb/ref 1069 "e-9704" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175885 #edb/ref 1071 "At full speed, a fully grown cheetah can cover a distance of $998$ feet in $10$ seconds. What is the speed of the cheetah when running at full speed?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175885 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "696213fa-757d-5450-906a-ffb0638599e8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175885 #edb/ref 1074 "Speed is a special unit rate applied to moving objects. It is defined as *the distance traveled per unit of time*:\n\n$$\n\\text{speed} = \\dfrac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{time}}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed in feet per second, we divide the number of feet, $998,$ by the number of seconds, $10.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{998}{10} & =99.8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the speed of the cheetah is $99.8$ feet per second." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175886 #edb/ref 1069 "e-9705" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175886 #edb/ref 1071 "Moving at a constant rate, it takes $8$ seconds for a particular type of fish to swim a distance of $200$ centimeters. Find the distance this fish can cover in $3$ seconds." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175886 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1c7eac8b-b163-532f-84f0-10ffd23a67f6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175886 #edb/ref 1074 "Speed is a special unit rate applied to moving objects. It is defined as *the distance traveled per unit of time*:\n\n$$\n\\text{speed} = \\dfrac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{time}}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed, in centimeters per second, we divide the number of centimeters, $200,$ by the number of seconds, $8.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{200}{8} & =200÷8 \\\\  & =25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the speed of the fish is $25$ centimeters per second. \n\nTo find the distance covered in $3$ seconds, we multiply the speed by $3.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{distance} & =\\text{speed}\\times \\text{time} \\\\  & =25\\times 3 \\\\  & =75.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fish can cover $75$ centimeters in $3$ seconds." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175887 #edb/ref 1069 "e-9706" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175887 #edb/ref 1071 "It takes $5$ days for the Earth to travel $13$ million kilometers around the Sun. How much time does it take for the Earth to travel $52$ million kilometers around the Sun?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175887 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "cb7d1f42-a5bc-5fba-834c-07a2ceb0644a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175887 #edb/ref 1074 "Speed is a special unit rate applied to moving objects. It is defined as *the distance traveled per unit of time*:\n\n$$\n\\text{speed} = \\dfrac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{time}}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed, in millions of kilometers per day, we divide the number of million kilometers, $13,$ by the number of days, $5.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{13}{5} & =13÷5 \\\\  & =2.6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the speed of the Earth is $2.6$ million kilometers per day. \n\nTo find the time it takes the Earth to cover $52$ million kilometers, we divide the distance by $2.6.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{time} & =\\frac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{speed}} \\\\  & =\\frac{52}{2.6} \\\\  & =\\frac{52\\times 10}{2.6\\times 10} \\\\  & =\\frac{520}{26} \\\\  & =520÷26 \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, it takes the Earth $20$ days to travel $52$ million kilometers around the Sun." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176030 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049143 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176030 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050051 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176030 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050273 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176030 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186176327 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176030 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186176328 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176030 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186268971 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176030 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186268975 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176030 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186268977 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176030 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186268980 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176030 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186268982 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176030 #edb/ref 1039 "Calculating the Speed of an Object" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [175921861